ubtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Who sets it:** Under Investment Company Act **Rule 22c-1(b)**, the fund's **board of directors** sets the time(s) of day when NAV is computed, and may change them. The time is disclosed in the prospectus/SAI.\n\n**Frequency:** NAV must be computed **at least once each business day (Monday–Friday)**. Exceptions are days with no portfolio trading that could materially affect NAV, days with no purchase or redemption orders, and customary holidays. Creations and redemptions are **forward-priced** at the next-computed NAV.\n\n**Status of 4 pm ET:** It is **industry convention, not a regulatory mandate**. It matches the NYSE's regular-session close, when most closing prices are set. Boards can choose other times, such as earlier on half-days. Extended or near-24-hour exchange trading does not change NAV timing. The SEC's 2022 proposal for a 4 pm \"hard close\" for mutual funds was not adopted.","ttft_ms":3116,"type":"result","duration_ms":6150,"uuid":"47c48b67-2905-4bb3-8905-a83ea40a45ed","ttft_stream_ms":490,"time_to_request_ms":70,"first_content_frame_ms":490,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
